 "upload": {
  "title": "Alberta Voted on Leaving Canada. What Now? #shorts",
  "description": "On October 19, 2026, voters in Alberta, home to the world's fourth-largest oil reserves, answered a referendum question on whether the province should remain in Canada or begin the legal process toward a binding separation vote. Ballots are counted by hand, so results come slowly. Pre-vote polling put support for starting the process around 23 percent; Premier Danielle Smith opposes leaving. Prime Minister Mark Carney called the vote a dangerous bluff and said the U.S. is trying to break Canada. The vote itself does not separate Alberta from Canada.\n\nSources:\nNPR: Alberta voters weigh future in Canada (Oct 18, 2026)\nPBS NewsHour: Prime Minister Mark Carney says U.S. is trying to break Canada as Alberta votes on separation path (Oct 2026)\nFortune: Alberta, home to the world's 4th-largest oil reserves, will vote on a first step to leaving Canada (Oct 17, 2026)\nNBC News: Mark Carney makes final appeal against Alberta separation ahead of referendum (Oct 2026)\nDawn / Reuters-style wire: Oil-rich Alberta vote to determine next step towards possible separation from Canada (Oct 2026)\n\n#geopolitics #Alberta #Canada #Carney #oil",
